# This CITATION.cff makes GitHub show a "Cite this repository" widget and lets
# citation managers read the software metadata. Zenodo reads .zenodo.json (not
# this file) when it mints the release DOI, so keep the two in sync.
#
# Both files currently describe the paper archive, which freezes the model and the
# case-study data used in the Frontiers hydrogen VPP paper. The archive has two
# versions on Zenodo: 10.5281/zenodo.21865130 is the GitHub release of tag
# v1.0.1-h2vppfcr, and 10.5281/zenodo.21867045 is the trimmed model-and-data
# upload the paper cites. The doi below is the concept DOI, which resolves to
# whichever is newest. Before the next ordinary software release, put the generic
# el1xr_opt title, abstract and version back, or that release will be labelled as
# a paper snapshot too.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: 'Model and data for "Market-driven co-sizing of a hybrid power-and-hydrogen virtual power plant for energy and frequency reserve markets"'
abstract: >-
  This release freezes the optimisation model and the case-study data used in the
  study "Market-driven co-sizing of a hybrid power-and-hydrogen virtual power plant
  for energy and frequency reserve markets" (Alvarez, Gutierrez-Guerra, and
  Ramos), so that every result in the paper can be reproduced from a fixed model
  version. The model, el1xr_opt, is an open-source mixed-integer linear
  optimization model, built in Pyomo, that co-optimizes the sizing (investment)
  and the operation of hybrid renewable energy systems coupling electricity and
  hydrogen, with unit commitment, storage, a pressure-resolved hydrogen network,
  and frequency containment reserve (FCR) provision. It extends the openTEPES
  modelling framework and ships automatic solver setup. The case-study data sit
  under data/H2VPPFCR/: the 2025 SE3 market series, the site wind, the
  hydrogen-demand profiles, the techno-economic parameters, the case builder, and
  the experiment configurations.
type: software
authors:
